                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] Experienced on the Oculus Rift with Touch Controllers [/h1]\n[i] Note for Oculus users: HTC  Vive wands show up as Touch controllers, but they basically work the same here [/i]\n\nI don't like downvoting free educational apps on Steam. However, this is a rather poor effort. Some of the translations are rough, but that's not even a reason I'm not recommending this. This just doesn't bring anything to VR, even at free, that I can recommend this to anyone. \n\nThe graphics are not there. You don't feel like you're in space or that you're viewing planets. I would be more impressed looking at one of those scale models that middle school students make for their science project. There's not many facts contained within the different models and they are just text anyway. Navigating the UI is clunky as well as teleporting around in space.\n\nI would recommend spending some money and either getting Discovering Space 2, Overview, or Titans of Space 2 (or Mission:ISS for free!). Better to have a good space experience than waste time on this free one. \n\nRate 4.5/10. I really didn't want to not recommend this game, but it's just not really good at all, brings very little of value. Time is valuable.",
